  "observations": [
    {
      "id": "DECAL-VS-INPUTS",
      "source": "unlit_decal_vs.vs-metal-0.ll:274-278",
      "observation": "Input float3 ATTR0 location0; PerFrameVertexCB buffer1/560bytes; ParticleDecalVS buffer7/144bytes: WORLD_MATRIX@0, WORLD_TO_UV_MATRIX@64, PROJECTION_Y_RANGE@128."
    },
    {
      "id": "DECAL-VS-POSITION-UV",
      "source": "unlit_decal_vs.vs-metal-0.ll:26-123,150-235",
      "observation": "Homogeneous input transforms by DECAL_WORLD_MATRIX. U=dot(world,UVstoredVector0); V=1-dot(world,UVstoredVector2); clip uses VIEW_PROJECTION_MATRIX, not mProj. No shader flatten-to-ground or sampling of terrain/depth; terrain triangle selection/world matrix setup are CPU unknowns."
    },
    {
      "id": "DECAL-VS-FADE",
      "source": "unlit_decal_vs.vs-metal-0.ll:124-145",
      "observation": "gap=abs(world.y-Y_RANGE.x). Fade=1 if gap<=Y_RANGE.y, else1-(gap-Y_RANGE.y)/Y_RANGE.z. Vertex computed/interpolated. No epsilon guard or saturation in VS."
    },
    {
      "id": "DECAL-PS-COLOR",
      "source": "unlit_decal_ps.ps-metal-0.ll:10-30,64-69",
      "observation": "L=sample(diffuse,UV)*sample(particleLookup,COLOR_UV.xy)*MODULATE_COLOR. Output.rgb=L.rgb, output.a=L.a*max(interpolatedFade,0). No global remap stage or RGB clamp in selected native code. DiffuseTex0/Smp0; lookupTex1/Smp1; LocalsFragment buffer16/32bytes: COLOR_UV@0,MODULATE_COLOR@16."
    },
    {
      "id": "DECAL-PS-PALETTE",
      "source": "unlit_decal_ps.ps-metal-11.ll:10-38,77-84",
      "observation": "Base RGBA B -> palette at[clamp(dot(B,cPaletteSrcMixerMain),0,1),cPaletteSelectMain.x]+select.zw. Replace only B.rgb with palette.rgb; preserve B.a. Multiply lookup then MODULATE_COLOR; alpha-only max(fade,0). LocalsFragment16/64bytes: select@0,mixer@16,COLOR_UV@32,MODULATE_COLOR@48. PaletteTex0/Smp0,diffuseTex1/Smp1,lookupTex2/Smp2."
    },
    {
      "id": "DECAL-FOW",
      "source": "unlit_decal_vs.vs-metal-1.ll:237-243;unlit_decal_ps.ps-metal-8.ll:25-34",
      "observation": "VS derives FOW UV from transformed world.xz*FOG_OF_WAR_PARAMS.xy+zw. Default PS multiplies RGB only by FOW sample alpha; height fade affects output alpha. Adds FOWTex0/Smp15; shifts diffuse and lookup textures to1/2, retains diffuse/lookup samplers0/1."
    },
    {
      "id": "DECAL-FOW-PALETTE",
      "source": "unlit_decal_ps.ps-metal-38.ll:10-53,95-104",
      "observation": "Combined palette/FOW route preserves diffuse alpha, multiplies lookup/modulation, applies max(interpolated fade,0) to alpha and FOW alpha only to RGB. FOW/palette/diffuse/lookup textures0/1/2/3; palette/diffuse/lookup samplers0/1/2 and FOWsampler15."
    }
  ],
